# --- Backlog: schema vs content ------------------------------------------------
# The backlog is two different kinds of artefact under one directory, with two
# different owners. GitHub applies the LAST matching rule, so the more specific
# schema/tooling rules are listed after the directory rule above.
#
#   * SCHEMA + TOOLING (architecture-owned): the shape of a ticket, the enum of
#     statuses/labels/epic keys, the validator and its fixtures. Changing these
#     changes every ticket in the repo and every agent that parses one, so
#     @CandleViewer/architecture is the required approver. QA review is welcome
#     but not blocking.
#   * CONTENT (QA-owned): the individual ticket .json files — acceptance criteria,
#     black-box test plans, DoR/DoD evidence. @CandleViewer/qa is the required
#     approver because DoR/DoD self-sufficiency (C-11.1) is a QA judgement;
#     architecture review is welcome but not blocking.
#
# A PR that touches BOTH the schema and ticket content needs both owners, which
# is intentional — split it (C-4.6) unless the content change is a mechanical
# migration required by the schema change, in which case label it `shared-package`
# and get both approvals.
# future: E02/later scaffolding; directory does not exist yet.
/docs/plan/backlog/schema/               @CandleViewer/architecture
# future: E02/later scaffolding; directory does not exist yet.
